    const r9Rule=()=>`<div class="tt-rule"><h3>How tutoring changes GPA</h3><p>Each student needs a particular amount of tutoring to keep their GPA at 3.50. Exactly that amount keeps it unchanged. Less tutoring lowers their GPA; extra tutoring raises it.</p><p>For the same number of minutes, too little tutoring lowers GPA more than extra tutoring raises it. For example, 4 minutes too little gives a GPA of 3.38, whereas 4 extra minutes gives 3.56.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Time compared with actual tutoring need</th><th>Final GPA</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>25 minutes short</td><td>3.20</td></tr><tr><td>4 minutes short</td><td>3.38</td></tr><tr><td>Exactly enough</td><td>3.50</td></tr><tr><td>4 extra minutes</td><td>3.56</td></tr><tr><td>25 extra minutes</td><td>3.65</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These are the supplied rules for this fictional game. They stay the same across rounds.</p></div>`;
